{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.MonoidAlgebra.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.ToLin","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Perm","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JucysMurphyCoeff"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.trace_centralC2_eq_factorial_mul_choose_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.trace_centralC2_eq_factorial_mul_choose_two","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepTrace.lean#L88-L102","doc":"**Identity (B), coefficient side, general `n`, ℂ-free.** The trace of the Jucys–Murphy central\nelement `C₂` acting by left multiplication on the regular representation `R[S_n]` is\n`n! · binom(n,2)`, over **any** `CommRing R`. Combines the general trace formula\n(`trace_mulLeft_eq_card_mul_coeff_one`: `tr_reg(z) = |S_n|·z(1)`), the order `|S_n| = n!`\n(`Fintype.card_perm` + `Fintype.card_fin`), and the identity coefficient `C₂(1) = binom(n,2)`\n(`centralC2_coeff_one`). This is side 1 of the Identity-(B) trace equation; equating it with the\nWedderburn block side `Σ_λ dim(λ)²·Σ_{c∈λ} c(c)²` (formalised conditionally in `RegularRepBlockTrace`,\nthe residual input being the S_n Okounkov–Vershik identification) yields (B). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2_coeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2_coeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepTrace.lean#L83-L86","doc":"The identity coefficient of `centralC2` is `binom(n,2)` (re-exported from the merged\nℂ-free core `JucysMurphyCoeff.centralC2_coeff_one`; the two agree by definitional unfolding). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.centralC2","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepTrace.lean#L76-L81","doc":"The Jucys–Murphy central element `C₂ = Σ_k X_k²`, `X_k = Σ_{i<k}(i k)`, as a named element of\n`R[S_n] = MonoidAlgebra R (Perm (Fin n))`. This is the exact expression whose identity coefficient\nis computed by `JucysMurphyCoeff.centralC2_coeff_one`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.trace_mulLeft_eq_card_mul_coeff_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RegularRepTrace.trace_mulLeft_eq_card_mul_coeff_one","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RegularRepTrace.lean#L56-L74","doc":"**Trace of the left regular representation reads off the identity coefficient.**\nFor a finite group `G` and `z ∈ R[G] = MonoidAlgebra R G` over any `CommRing R`, the trace of\nleft-multiplication by `z` on the regular representation is `|G| · z(1)`. Proof: in the basis of\n`single g 1` (`Finsupp.basisSingleOne`), the matrix of `LinearMap.mulLeft R z` has `(i,j)` entry\n`(z * single j 1) i = z(i · j⁻¹)` (`MonoidAlgebra.mul_single_apply`), so every diagonal entry is\n`z(j · j⁻¹) = z(1)`; summing the constant diagonal over the `|G|` basis vectors gives `|G|·z(1)`.\nNo field, no representation theory — pure group-algebra/linear-algebra over generic `R`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}